WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:02.732
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.990
- Vegas is like constantly
living under stage lights.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.850
Vegas is like the old-time, big movie set,

00:00:13.850 --> 00:00:18.690
and Vegas' relationship
with drag is fantastic.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.910
Whether it's a showgirl on the strip

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.010
or a showgirl who happens
to be a boy in a night club,

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.710
we're all entertaining people

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.653
and this town loves entertainment.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:29.810
- I'm Alex Serpa.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:31.100
- I'm Daniel HoneyCutt.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.370
We're the Queens of Las Vegas,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:34.530
and we host What a Drag.
- And we host “What a Drag.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:37.873
- [Both] The longest-running
drag show in Las Vegas.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.190
- What a Drag started in 1996.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:51.400
It's everything in Vegas,
everything in Hollywood,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.640
everything on Broadway,
all converted to drag.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.030
Our show is the three C's:

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:01.365
costume, character, and comedy.

00:01:01.365 --> 00:01:04.970
- The fact that we're a couple,
I think, is the reason why

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.490
Queens of Las Vegas
has managed to persist,

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:10.940
'cause we're a unified
front running the show.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:14.200
When I was a kid, I would
play in my mom's pumps.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.810
As I got older and I wanted to do drag,

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.170
my mother bought me my very first dress.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.860
She saw that drag could be
a creative outlet for me

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.580
that would help me develop as a person.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:27.360
I met Alex at 20, and I,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.380
all those years I had been studying drag,

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:31.520
and Alex told me,

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.580
“I see something in you,” you know?

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.575
He came up with the idea of
doing a duet and he said,

00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:38.210
“We’ll do it together, that
way if you get scared,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.620
“I’m standing next to you.”

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:43.400
- When I told him I can
see something in you,

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.816
what I was really thinkin',

00:01:44.816 --> 00:01:48.070
I found somebody to do all those duets

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:50.053
that I've always wanted to do.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.600
- When I start doing my makeup,

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.940
I have to start with
blocking out my eyebrows,

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:58.010
not that I have much left.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:58.843
- [Alex] Smooth it out.

00:01:58.843 --> 00:01:59.820
- [Daniel] Yeah, and from there

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:01.490
it's about creating contour.

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.136
- [Alex] A contour is a permanent shadow.

00:02:04.136 --> 00:02:06.800
- [Daniel] And from there
you move on to eyes.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.350
- [Alex] Eyebrows are really important.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.450
- [Daniel] Fake eyelashes.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.400
- [Alex] Fake eyelashes.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.030
- [Daniel] They're always
better the second time.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:12.950
- [Alex] Lip shaping.

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:13.783
- Oh, yes.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.170
The shape of a lip, it's very important.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:17.480
- [Alex] The shape of a lip.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:18.313
Padding.

00:02:18.313 --> 00:02:19.510
The hip pads are shaped

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:24.510
like Africa and South
America respectively.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.250
They're not just hip pads,
they're also butt pads.

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.400
- What I look for in a wig is character.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.000
And I'm partial to being blonde.

00:02:33.948 --> 00:02:36.531
(upbeat music)

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:41.410
- Whatever number you're performing,

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:42.810
you gotta have a gimmick.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:45.290
The gimmick's gotta last
you all four minutes.

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.060
- [Daniel] Chyna Nicole is a showgirl.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.000
- [Alex] Anye Gotti, she's unstoppable.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.023
- Danielle Steelcox,
she's the future of drag.

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:58.390
And Alex and I being a
couple and both doing drag

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:02.070
and hosting the show, we are
family and then we're also

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:05.613
a drag family, so I've always
had a sisterhood around me.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.330
When you come to Vegas,
whether you're a local

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:13.470
or you're a tourist, you
get to be your true self.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.500
- [Alex] There's never a boring moment.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:18.750
- [Daniel] What a Drag is like Las Vegas

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.610
because we don't have limits,

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:21.903
just like Las Vegas.

